Black & White Decompilation @PROJECT_VERSION@
==========================================

A fan-made decompilation of Lionhead's Black & White (2001) that runs the game on current Windows with its old
problems fixed: SafeDisc, the "You need DirectX 7" check, crashes at start-up and at high resolutions, hangs when
quitting, the disc requirement and more. It also adds a Direct3D 9 renderer: native widescreen resolutions such as
2560x1440, windowed and borderless modes, anti-aliasing, and texture packs.

The game is not included. You need your own installed copy of Black & White.


Requirements
------------
- Windows 10 or 11.
- Black & White 1.00 (English), installed.
- The unprotected runblack.exe. The retail runblack.exe is wrapped in SafeDisc, whose driver current Windows refuses
  to load, so it cannot start. The decompilation supports the unprotected build of the same version, from the disc's
  crack folder (SHA-256 86a30b08ab2ea8a240403d37f8f0303cf65aa5cde8e7f673049ab01654ccf755). BWLaunch.exe checks
  runblack.exe and tells you if it is a different one. The official patches 1.1 and 1.2 are not supported yet.
- The disc or a mounted disc image, or else the disc's Audio folder copied into the game folder.


Installing
----------
Run BWDecomp-@PROJECT_VERSION@-Setup.exe and choose the Black & White folder (the one with runblack.exe). Setup adds
these files and changes none of the game's:

    BWLaunch.exe    starts the game with the fixes
    BWDecomp.dll    the decompiled code, the fixes and the renderer
    BWDecomp.ini    settings (kept when you update)
    BWDecomp\       this file, the documentation and the uninstaller

Setup asks for administrator rights only if the game folder needs them (for example below Program Files).

Without setup: copy BWLaunch.exe, BWDecomp.dll and BWDecomp.ini from the zip into the game folder.


Playing
-------
Start the game with the "Black & White (Decompilation)" shortcut, or BWLaunch.exe in the game folder. Starting
runblack.exe directly runs the game without any of the fixes.


Settings
--------
BWDecomp.ini in the game folder; each setting is explained there. Some favourites:

    [Display] WindowMode       0 full screen, 1 window, 2 borderless window covering the screen
    [Display] AntiAliasing     4 or 8 for smoother edges (0 = off)
    [Display] Anisotropy       16 for sharper ground in the distance (0 = off)
    [Display] VSync            1 = no tearing
    [Diagnostics] ScreenshotKey  123 = F12 saves PNG screenshots to Screenshots\
    [Textures] Replace         texture packs from Textures\Replace\ (see TEXTURES.md)

The game's own settings, such as the screen resolution and the detail level, stay where the game keeps them:
HKEY_CURRENT_USER\Software\Lionhead Studios Ltd\Black & White\BWSetup.

BWDecomp\BWDecomp.default.ini is a copy of the settings as shipped with this version.


Problems
--------
BWDecomp.log in the game folder says what happened; include it when you report a problem. Every fix can be switched
off in BWDecomp.ini; FIXES.md explains each one.


Uninstalling
------------
Settings > Apps > Black & White Decompilation, or BWDecomp\Uninstall.exe. Only what setup installed is removed. A
BWDecomp.ini you changed, your saved games, screenshots and texture packs stay. If you copied the files from the zip
by hand, delete them by hand.


Documentation (in this folder)
------------------------------
    FIXES.md       every fix, its cause and its setting
    RENDERER.md    the Direct3D 9 renderer
    TEXTURES.md    making texture packs
    CHANGELOG.md   what changed in each version


Black & White is a game by Lionhead Studios. This project is not affiliated with or endorsed by Lionhead Studios or
